                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                        "entry_id": "e122bc95-6da8-3894-877a-39708116f895",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In an untoward way."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "25c19841-704e-45e8-a7f4-79ae71be700a",
                                "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                                "text": "Those ruddy plumes, embrew′d with heavenly food, / When I would suck them, twine to driest coral; / And when I couch between her lily buds, / They surge like frothy water mounts above all: / Surely, they were all made unto good uses, / But she them all untowardly abuses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e74e4b33-ea17-42cb-98dc-754209e6d478",
                                "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                                "text": "O day untowardly turned!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d77d2422-a073-43cb-a164-b8ac973524b0",
                                "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                                "text": "[…] whenever my brains come to be dissected, you will perceive, without spectacles, that he has left a large uneven thread, as you sometimes see in an unsaleable piece of cambrick, running along the whole length of the web, and so untowardly, you cannot so much as cut out a * *, (here I hang up a couple of lights again)—or a fillet, or a thumb-stall, but it is seen or felt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fcdf7674-cf4e-4c64-8ccf-68eaed6340af",
                                "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                                "text": "“[…] I have observed, Mrs. Elton, in the course of my life, that if things are going untowardly one month, they are sure to mend the next.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "715277f1-a643-4749-b86a-bc696a9b2293",
                                "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                                "text": "It has been said that Mr. Slope, as he started for Ullathorne, received a dispatch from his friend, Mr. Towers, which had the effect of putting him in that high good-humour which subsequent events somewhat untowardly damped."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9def481-f931-4492-b820-6ea83d7c106e",
                                "sense_id": "34bb94ee-01bb-34af-9706-35e4e84780d1",
                                "text": "Perhaps that’s because discretion is a restaurateur’s asset—to dish untowardly would be bad for business."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
